    {
      "index": 2,
      "label": "Parse individual records",
      "intent": "Implement `parse_record(line)` to validate one complete record and return its normalized dictionary.\n- The input must contain exactly six `|`-separated fields in this order: `TYPE|RECORD_ID|ORDER_ID|AMOUNT|CURRENCY|TIMESTAMP`.\n- `TYPE` is case-insensitive `ORDER` or `PAYMENT` and is stored uppercase.\n- Trim both identifiers; both must remain non-empty, and every `ORDER_ID` must start with the exact prefix `ORD-`.\n- The currency must be exactly `USD`; process only `USD` records.\n- The timestamp must use `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM` or `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS` with valid calendar values.\n- Use integer cents from `parse_amount(s)`; negative orders are invalid.\n- Return exactly the keys `type`, `record_id`, `order_id`, `amount`, `currency`, and `timestamp`, or return `None` for any invalid record.\n- Invalid input must be skipped by the caller without raising or printing.",
      "checkHint": "`parse_record('order|r1| ORD-7 |12.50|USD|2024-01-01 09:00')` should return a normalized record with type `ORDER` and amount `1250`.",
