      "checkHint": "Loading two valid rows with the same `record_id` must retain only the first; a payment of `-250` for an existing order contributes `250` to `compute_refunds(records)`.",
      "timeShare": 20
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "label": "Match payments to orders",
      "intent": "Implement `match_payments(records)` to create one result for every retained order, in retained order-record order.\n- Records use integer cents, `USD`, normalized timestamps, and the exact keys returned by `parse_record(line)`.\n- A non-refund payment qualifies only for the order with the same `order_id` and only when its timestamp is from the order timestamp through a time strictly less than 72 hours after it.\n- **The order timestamp is included, but a payment exactly 72 hours later is outside the window.**\n- Refunds, meaning negative payments, never match.\n- If several payments qualify, select the earliest payment timestamp; for an exact timestamp tie, select retained source order.\n- Each result has exactly `order_id`, `status`, and `amount`.\n- A matched result uses lowercase status `matched` and the selected payment amount; an unmatched result uses lowercase status `unmatched` and amount `0`.\n- Do not mutate records or use global state.",
      "checkHint": "An otherwise qualifying payment exactly 72 hours after its order must produce an `unmatched` result.",
      "timeShare": 25
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "label": "Build the summary",
      "intent": "Implement `build_summary(matches, refund_total)` to return the final report dictionary.\n- Return exactly five keys: `total_orders`, `matched_count`, `refund_total`, `net_total`, and `unmatched_ids`.\n- `total_orders` is the number of supplied match results.\n- `matched_count` counts only results whose status is exactly lowercase `matched`.\n- `refund_total` is the supplied qualifying refund total in integer cents.\n- `net_total` is matched payment amounts minus `refund_total`; if this calculation is below zero, report `0`.\n- `unmatched_ids` contains unmatched order IDs only, deduplicated and sorted in ascending lexicographic order.\n- Return values must not mutate input objects or depend on global state.",
      "checkHint": "For one matched amount of `500` and `refund_total` of `700`, the summary must report `net_total` as `0`.",
      "timeShare": 15
    }
  ]
}

